/**
\page devs_generator Generator DEVS atomic model

\tableofcontents

\section generator_overview Overview

Periodic job source. While `active` it emits a new `Job` on `out` every
`period` time units; any message on `stop` makes it `passive` for good.

| | |
|---|---|
| Kind | Atomic DEVS model |
| Formalism | Parallel DEVS (PythonPDEVS) |
| Language / framework | Python / PythonPDEVS (pypdevs) |
| Source | `gen_proc.py` ( \ref gen_proc.Generator ) |
| Parameters | `name` (default `"gen"`), `period` (default 2.0) |
| Initial state | phase `active`, sigma = period, count = 0 |

\section generator_formal Formal specification

    M = < X, Y, S, delta_int, delta_ext, delta_con, lambda, ta >

- X = { (p, v) : p in InPorts, v in X_p } with InPorts = { stop }
- Y = { (p, v) : p in OutPorts, v in Y_p } with OutPorts = { out }
- S = { active, passive } x R0+ (sigma) x N (count)
- ta, delta_int, delta_ext, delta_con and lambda are tabulated in the sections below.

\section generator_ports Ports

\subsection generator_inports Input ports

| Port | Value type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `stop` | any | any message silences the generator |

\subsection generator_outports Output ports

| Port | Value type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `out` | `Job` | the job emitted at the end of each period |

\section generator_state State

\subsection generator_phases Phases

| Phase | ta(s) | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `active` | period | counting down to the next job |
| `passive` | inf | stopped, no further output |

\subsection generator_vars State variables

| Variable | Type | Initial value | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `phase` | `str` | `"active"` | discrete phase |
| `sigma` | `float` | period | remaining time in the current phase |
| `count` | `int` | 0 | id of the next job, incremented per emission |

The variables are held in \ref gen_proc.GeneratorState "GeneratorState".

\section generator_ta Time advance ta(s)

`ta(s) = sigma`: `period` while active, `INFINITY` once passive.

\section generator_dint Internal transition delta_int(s)

| From phase | To phase | Action |
|---|---|---|
| `active` | `active` | count += 1; sigma = period |

`passive` has ta = inf, so delta_int is never invoked there.

\section generator_dext External transition delta_ext(s, e, x)

| From phase | Port | Condition | To phase | Action |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `active` | `stop` | a message is present | `passive` | sigma = INFINITY |
| `passive` | `stop` | a message is present | `passive` | sigma = INFINITY (no change) |

In PythonPDEVS the elapsed time e is `self.elapsed` inside `extTransition`.
The source also has an else branch (`sigma -= e` when nothing arrived on
`stop`), which is unreachable because `stop` is the only input port.

\section generator_dcon Confluent transition delta_con(s, x)

Not overridden. PythonPDEVS applies the framework default: delta_int first,
then delta_ext with e = 0. A `stop` arriving exactly when a job is due is
processed after that job is emitted.

\section generator_lambda Output function lambda(s)

| Phase | Port | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `active` | `out` | `Job(count)` |

\section generator_diagram State diagram

Solid edges are internal transitions (fired when ta(s) expires); dashed edges
are external transitions (fired on input). Labels use `trigger / action`.

\dot
digraph generator_states {
    rankdir=LR;
    node [shape=ellipse, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10];
    edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9];
    __init [shape=point];
    active [label="active\n(ta = period)"];
    passive [label="passive\n(ta = inf)"];
    __init -> active;
    active -> active [label="int / emit Job(count), count += 1"];
    active -> passive [label="ext: stop / sigma = inf", style=dashed];
    passive -> passive [label="ext: stop / stay passive", style=dashed];
}
\enddot

\section generator_source Source mapping

| DEVS element | Implementation in `gen_proc.py` |
|---|---|
| Ports | \ref gen_proc.Generator.stop "Generator.stop", \ref gen_proc.Generator.out "Generator.out" (created in `__init__`) |
| State | \ref gen_proc.GeneratorState "GeneratorState" held in `Generator.state` |
| Initialization | \ref gen_proc.Generator.__init__ "Generator.__init__()" |
| ta | \ref gen_proc.Generator.timeAdvance "Generator.timeAdvance()" |
| delta_int | \ref gen_proc.Generator.intTransition "Generator.intTransition()" |
| delta_ext | \ref gen_proc.Generator.extTransition "Generator.extTransition()" |
| delta_con | inherited from `AtomicDEVS` (framework default) |
| lambda | \ref gen_proc.Generator.outputFnc "Generator.outputFnc()" |
*/
